/-!
# `Work.MotK.LinkCertT` — the T-twist link certificate of the Crauder–Katz transformation

Target of this file: `Work.MotK.LinkCertT`, the K-route deliverable `LK_T` of
`MOTIVIC_S45_LEAD.md` §6 / `Submission/Work/MotK/GUIDE_LINK.md` §B: an affine certificate
`Work.MotV.LinkCert (RatFunc 𝕜) (twistFieldT D hT) (twistFieldT D (hT^2))` for the T-twist of the
Klein curve.

## What is proved here

Two of the *junk* conditions of the certificate's census are discharged in elementary
(and completely general) form:

* `GeomRuled_ratFunc_self`: the rational function field `K(t)` is geometrically ruled over `K`
  (the identity embedding is non-constant at `t`) — the "junk" criterion for the rational
  divisors of the census;
* `JunkClass_of_resF_ratFunc_ratFunc`: a codimension-one point of `𝔸ⁿ_K` whose residue field is
  `K(t)(z) = RatFunc (RatFunc K)` is junk — the criterion for the coordinate hyperplane primes
  (`F = x₀` in the certificate) and for the "cone/plane classes" of the paper's census.

## The remaining inputs (audit)

The certificate asks for `F, G ∈ K[x₀,x₁,x₂]` (`K = RatFunc 𝕜`) with

1. `Φ : Localization.Away F ≃ₐ[K] Localization.Away G` (the two charts of the Cremona map);
2. a height-one prime `zP ∋ G` with `resF K zP ≅ RatFunc F₁` and *all other* height-one primes
   above `G` junk;
3. every height-one prime above `F` either `≅ RatFunc F₂` or junk.

Conditions 2 and 3 are *elementary* once one two-generator presentation of the twist fields is
known: `RatFunc F₁` is the fraction field of `K[x]/(G₁)` for `G₁` the generator of the kernel of
`K[X₀,X₁,X₂] → RatFunc F₁`, `X₀ ↦ u`, `X₁ ↦ v`, `X₂ ↦ RatFunc.X`, with `F₁ = K(u,v)`
(any function field of transcendence degree one is generated by two elements); the same holds for
`F₂`, and for `F` one may take any polynomial all of whose prime factors are junk (e.g. `x₀`).

The only genuinely transcendental condition is therefore **(1)**: an isomorphism between the two
"charts" `D(F)` and `D(G)` of `𝔸³_K` whose two boundary divisors are the cylinders over the twists
`C_h` and `C_{h²}`.  *That* is the content of the Crauder–Katz quadro-cubic link
(Crauder–Katz Thm 2.2(ii), Lin–Shinder `prop:elliptic`): `Φ` is induced by the quadro-cubic
Cremona map `f = P ∘ y` of `Submission/Work/MotK/LinkTwData`, whose two unit identities (the
T-twist of `Work.MotK.KleinLinkUnit` and its inverse) make `f^*` an isomorphism of the two
localisations.  Neither the map nor its divisor census can be manufactured algebraically: by
`IsEmpty`-type rigidity (`MOTIVIC_S45_LEAD.md` node `RIG`) the twist fields `F₁` and `F₂` are
non-isomorphic, so no automorphism-level isomorphism of the two charts exists, and every
"triangular"/Jonquières Cremona transformation only produces junk divisors.

**Warning for the K3_T design.**  The T-twisted analogue of the identity
**I3** `s'(P(y)) = s(y)²` — on which the split unit condition `KleinLinkUnit` rests — is *false*
for the twisted data of `KleinTwData`: with `a = 2, b = 3, h = 5, y = ![1,2,3,4,5]` one has
`kleinTwSDual (kleinTwP y) - kleinTwS y ^ 2 = 9603168615890764344720 ≠ 0` (it *does* vanish for
`h = 1`).  Hence the twisted unit identity cannot simply mirror `KleinLinkUnit`; the normalisation
of the twisted `s'`/`R` must be settled (compare the inverse twist `z_j = w^{4j}y_j` used for
`kleinTwR`).  See `Submission/Work/MotK/AUDIT_LinkCertT.md` for the details and the exact
reduction of the certificate.
-/

namespace Work.MotK

open Work.MotV

open Work.MotV

/-- **The rational function field is geometrically ruled over itself.**  The identity
`RatFunc K →ₐ[K] RatFunc K` is non-constant at `RatFunc.X`: `RatFunc.X` is not in the image of
the constants, by `intDegree_C = 0 ≠ 1 = intDegree_X`.

This is the junk criterion used in the census of the Crauder–Katz link for the rational
(birational-to-`ℙ¹ × 𝔸¹`) divisors: it instantiates the definition
`Work.MotV.GeomRuled K F₀ = ∃ M, ∃ ι : F₀ →ₐ[K] RatFunc M, ∃ x, ∀ c : M, algebraMap M _ c ≠ ι x`
with `F₀ = M = K(t)`. -/
theorem GeomRuled_ratFunc_self (K : Type) [Field K] :
    GeomRuled K (RatFunc K) := by
  refine ⟨K, ?_, ?_, ?_, RatFunc.X, ?_⟩
  · infer_instance
  · infer_instance
  · exact AlgHom.id K (RatFunc K)
  · intro c hc
    have h2 : (RatFunc.C c : RatFunc K) = RatFunc.X := by
      simpa [RatFunc.algebraMap_eq_C] using hc
    have hdeg := congrArg (RatFunc.intDegree (K := K)) h2
    rw [RatFunc.intDegree_C, RatFunc.intDegree_X] at hdeg
    exact one_ne_zero hdeg.symm

/-- **The coordinate-hyperplane primes are junk.**  A codimension-one point of `𝔸ⁿ_K` whose
residue field is `K(t)(z)` (the rational surface `𝔸¹ × 𝔸¹`) satisfies `JunkClass`: take
`F₀ = RatFunc K` in `Work.MotV.JunkClass K x = ∃ F₀, GeomRuled K F₀ ∧ Nonempty (resF K x ≃ₐ[K]
RatFunc F₀)` and use `GeomRuled_ratFunc_self`.

This discharges the junk conditions of the census for `F = x₀` on the source side and for the
"cone/plane classes" of the target side (both have rational residue fields). -/
theorem JunkClass_of_resF_ratFunc_ratFunc (K : Type) [Field K] {n : ℕ}
    (x : Work.MotA.polySpec K n)
    (hx : Nonempty (Work.MotV.resF K x ≃ₐ[K] RatFunc (RatFunc K))) :
    JunkClass K x :=
  ⟨RatFunc K, inferInstance, inferInstance, GeomRuled_ratFunc_self K, hx⟩

/-- **`JunkClass` is a property of the residue field.**  If the residue fields of two
codimension-one points are `K`-isomorphic, junkness transfers.  This is the bookkeeping step
used in the class separation of the census: a divisor is junk if *any* of the points presenting
its class is. -/
theorem JunkClass_of_resF_algEquiv {K : Type} [Field K] {n : ℕ} {x y : Work.MotA.polySpec K n}
    (h : Nonempty (Work.MotV.resF K x ≃ₐ[K] Work.MotV.resF K y)) (hy : JunkClass K y) :
    JunkClass K x := by
  obtain ⟨F₀, hfield, halg, hgr, he⟩ := hy
  exact ⟨F₀, hfield, halg, hgr, ⟨(Classical.choice h).trans (Classical.choice he)⟩⟩

/-! ## The twisted polar form

`kleinTwQ = kleinTwP0` is a homogeneous quadratic form, so its polar form `kleinTwBilin` is
bilinear.  This is the first ingredient of the T-twisted link unit condition (the companion
stereographic identity is `Work.MotK.KleinTwBilinStereo` in the sibling file); it is *not* enough
on its own — see the warning in the module docstring and `AUDIT_LinkCertT.md` §3 on the failure of
the twisted analogue of I3. -/

/-- Bilinearity of the twisted polar form in its second argument (the polarisation identity for a
homogeneous quadratic form). -/
theorem kleinTwBilin_smul_right {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (a b h : R) (u v : Fin 5 → R) (c : R) :
    Work.MotK.kleinTwBilin a b h u (fun i => c * v i) = c * Work.MotK.kleinTwBilin a b h u v := by
  simp only [Work.MotK.kleinTwBilin, Work.MotK.kleinTwQ, Work.MotK.kleinTwP0, Pi.add_apply]
  first | refl_ring1 | ring

/-- **The principal primes of `𝔸ⁿ_K` have coheight one.**  Immediate from the proved
`Work.MotA.coheight_eq_one_iff` (`n` arbitrary, `K` a field): a prime element `p` of the UFD
`K[x₀,…,x_{n-1}]` spans a height-one prime.  This certifies the `zP_ht` field of the link
certificate whenever the distinguished point is presented as `primePoint K p hp`. -/
theorem coheight_primePoint {K : Type} [Field K] {n : ℕ} (p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) K)
    (hp : Prime p) :
    Order.coheight (Work.MotA.primePoint K p hp) = 1 :=
  (Work.MotA.coheight_eq_one_iff K n _).mpr ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩

/-! ## The two affine charts of the T-twisted link, as `K`-algebra maps

The link `f = kleinTwP ∘ kleinTwStereo : {v₀ = 0} ⇢ {w₀ = 0}` and its inverse
`χ = π_p ∘ kleinTwR` are read in the affine charts `chart3 = ![0,x₀,x₁,x₂,1]` of
`TwAmbh.lean`.  Their chart-coordinate functions are the rational functions

  `φ_j = f̂_{j+1}/f̂₄`,   `η_j = ǧ_{j+1}/ǧ₄`   (`j : Fin 3`),

so that `Φ := η^*` (the pullback along the inverse chart map) and `Ψ := φ^*` are `K`-algebra
endomorphisms of `Frac K[x₀,x₁,x₂]`.  `ChartCompC` states that they are mutually inverse on the
coordinate generators; that is the algebraic core (`A4`) of the chart isomorphism of the
certificate. -/

/-- The affine chart `v₄ = 1` of the hyperplane `{v₀ = 0} ⊂ ℙ⁴`, with coordinates
`(v₁,v₂,v₃) ↦ (x₀,x₁,x₂)`: `chartC = ![0, x₀, x₁, x₂, 1]`. -/
noncomputable def chartC (K : Type*) [CommRing K] : Fin 5 → MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K :=
  ![0, MvPolynomial.X 0, MvPolynomial.X 1, MvPolynomial.X 2, 1]

/-- A `K`-rational point of the twisted quadric `{q = 0}` with non-zero first coordinate,
`p = (1, 0, 1, b/(a·h), 0)`. -/
noncomputable def pointC (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) : Fin 5 → K
  | 0 => 1
  | 1 => 0
  | 2 => 1
  | 3 => b / (a * h)
  | 4 => 0

/-- The point `pointC` lies on the twisted quadric (over `K`). -/
theorem kleinTwQ_pointC_K (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) (ha : a ≠ 0) (hh : h ≠ 0) :
    kleinTwQ a b h (pointC K a b h) = 0 := by
  simp only [kleinTwQ, kleinTwP0, pointC]
  field_simp
  first | refl_ring1 | ring

/-- Evaluating the twisted quadric on constant polynomial coordinates. -/
theorem kleinTwQ_Cr (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) (p : Fin 5 → K) :
    kleinTwQ (MvPolynomial.C a : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C h)
      (fun i => (MvPolynomial.C (p i) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K)) =
        MvPolynomial.C (kleinTwQ a b h p) := by
  simp only [kleinTwQ, kleinTwP0, map_mul, map_pow, map_neg, map_add, map_sub]

/-- The point `pointC`, as a constant vector in the chart ring. -/
noncomputable def pRaC (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) : Fin 5 → MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K :=
  fun i => MvPolynomial.C (pointC K a b h i)

/-- The dehomogenised components `f̂ᵢ` of the forward chart map `f = kleinTwP ∘ kleinTwStereo`. -/
noncomputable def fhatC (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) (i : Fin 5) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K :=
  kleinTwP (MvPolynomial.C a) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C h)
    (kleinTwStereo (MvPolynomial.C a) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C h)
      (pRaC K a b h) (chartC K)) i

/-- The dehomogenised components `ǧᵢ` of the inverse chart map `π_p ∘ kleinTwR`. -/
noncomputable def ghatC (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) (i : Fin 5) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K :=
  kleinTwPi (pRaC K a b h)
    (kleinTwR (MvPolynomial.C a) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C h) (chartC K)) i

/-- The source divisor of the affine T-twisted link: `F_hom` dehomogenised to the chart
`{v₀ = 0, v₄ = 1}` at the point `pointC`: `GambC = b(p,v)·s(y(v))`, of degree 11 in `(x₀,x₁,x₂)`.
It is the `LinkCert` field `G`; the certificate has to multiply it by the strict transform `f̂₄`
of the target hyperplane (see `AUDIT_LinkCertT.md` §7). -/
noncomputable def GambC (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K :=
  kleinTwFhom (MvPolynomial.C a) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C h)
    (pRaC K a b h) (chartC K)

/-- The target divisor of the affine T-twisted link: `G_hom = b(p,R w)·s'(w)` dehomogenised to the
chart `{w₀ = 0, w₄ = 1}` at the point `pointC`, of degree 8.  It is the `LinkCert` field `F`. -/
noncomputable def FambC (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K :=
  kleinTwGhom' (MvPolynomial.C a) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C h)
    (pRaC K a b h) (chartC K)

/-- The point `pointC` lies on the twisted quadric, in the chart ring. -/
theorem kleinTwQ_pRaC (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) (ha : a ≠ 0) (hh : h ≠ 0) :
    kleinTwQ (MvPolynomial.C a) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C h) (pRaC K a b h) = 0 := by
  rw [show pRaC K a b h = fun i => (MvPolynomial.C (pointC K a b h i) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K) from rfl, kleinTwQ_Cr, kleinTwQ_pointC_K K a b h ha hh,
    MvPolynomial.C_0]

/-- The fraction field of the chart ring. -/
abbrev FracC (K : Type*) [Field K] := FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K)

/-- The chart-coordinate functions of the forward link map: `φ_j = f̂_{j+1}/f̂₄`. -/
noncomputable def phiCh (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) (j : Fin 3) : FracC K :=
  algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K) (FracC K) (fhatC K a b h ⟨j.val + 1, by omega⟩) *
    (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K) (FracC K) (fhatC K a b h 4))⁻¹

/-- The chart-coordinate functions of the inverse link map: `η_j = ǧ_{j+1}/ǧ₄`. -/
noncomputable def etaCh (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) (j : Fin 3) : FracC K :=
  algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K) (FracC K) (ghatC K a b h ⟨j.val + 1, by omega⟩) *
    (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K) (FracC K) (ghatC K a b h 4))⁻¹

/-- The pullback `Φ = η^*` along the inverse chart map, as a `K`-algebra map on the chart ring. -/
noncomputable def PhiCh (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K →ₐ[K] FracC K :=
  MvPolynomial.aeval (etaCh K a b h)

/-- The pullback `Ψ = φ^*` along the forward chart map. -/
noncomputable def PsiCh (K : Type*) [Field K] (a b h : K) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin 3) K →ₐ[K] FracC K :=
  MvPolynomial.aeval (phiCh K a b h)

end Work.MotK
